{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the fugitive came.</b> This is Og, who survived from the generation of the Flood. A midrashic aggadah: how did he live so long, from the days of Noah until Moses our master peace be upon him killed him? Because he intended that Abraham be killed and he would take Sarah, the Holy One blessed be He said to him: by your life, you receive the reward for your footsteps — that you live long in the world; but for plotting to kill the righteous man, by your life, you will see a thousand thousands and tens of thousands of myriads of his descendants, and that man's end will be to fall only by their hand, as it is written: 'And HaShem said to Moses: do not fear him' etc. — Bereshit Rabbah. And if you ask: how did Og survive? According to the one who says the inhabitants of the Land of Israel died from the heat of the Flood. And in Pirqei de-Rabbi Eliezer: this is Michael, for when the Holy One blessed be He cast down Samael and his host from the place of His holiness, he grabbed hold of Michael's wings to pull him down with him, and the Holy One blessed be He rescued him — therefore he is called 'fugitive,' and concerning him Ezekiel said: 'come to me, you who escaped.' And its plain sense: one man who escaped from the battle, and the verse is elliptical, like 'and he said to Joseph,' 'and he told Jacob,' and many others." "<b>And he was dwelling in the terebinths of Mamre.</b> As it is written above: 'and he dwelt in the terebinths of Mamre which are in Hebron.' Another interpretation: <b>and he</b> — the fugitive — <b>was dwelling in the terebinths of Mamre</b>; therefore he came to Abram to tell him." "<b>And they were Abram's covenant partners.</b> Therefore they went with him, as it is written: 'and the men who went with me, Aner, Eshkol, and Mamre.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The second midrash identifies the fugitive as Michael, using Ezekiel 14:22 (or possibly another passage) where the root פליט appears; the Hebrew citation 'בא אלי הפליט' is translated as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:16.789379467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}